      en: "Ras Laffan Industrial City, located on the northeast coast of Qatar, is the world's largest hub for liquefied natural gas (LNG). Established in 1996, the city covers an area of 295 square kilometers and hosts the entire value chain of the gas industry, from offshore production to liquefaction and export. The city is a cornerstone of the Qatari economy, contributing significantly to the nation's export revenues. Its key facilities include the massive LNG trains operated by Qatargas and RasGas, gas-to-liquids (GTL) plants like Pearl GTL and Oryx GTL, and petrochemical complexes. Ras Laffan Port is the largest artificial harbor in the world, specifically designed to handle exports of LNG, liquefied petroleum gas, GTL products, and sulfur. The city's infrastructure is continuously expanding to support growing production and secure Qatar's position as a leading energy exporter.",
